# Testing

## Hard rules (every non-docs PR)

- **Every behavioral change must ship with tests** — add or update Vitest coverage in the same PR.
- Missing tests = PR not ready for merge (see `AGENTS.md` Definition of Done).
- Pure docs / copy-only PRs: write **Tests: N/A** in the PR body; otherwise tests are required.
- Prefer extracting pure helpers into `lib/` (normalize, filter, guards, parsers) over untested branching inside React components.
- Feature agents must leave hooks for **test-dev**; orchestrator must schedule test-dev before treating the issue as done.

## What to test

- Unit-test pure logic in `lib/` (roles, rate-limit, hosts, site-settings normalize, featured-offer filters, etc.).
- Existing examples: `lib/role-utils.test.ts`, `lib/rate-limit.test.ts`, `lib/hosts.test.ts`.
- Prefer fixtures over live Sanity / Drive / Supabase network in unit tests.
- Keep suites fast and deterministic; do not call production CMS or banks in CI.
- When Playwright/e2e appears: smoke public home + one auth-gated happy path; keep e2e narrow.

## Commands

- `npm test` must pass locally before opening or updating a PR.
- CI runs the same suite — treat red CI as a blocker.
